At each decision the agent receives one new user message (step["seen"]): the simulation state (time, funds, payroll, runway, active and planned tasks) and, after time moves, the events since then. It also gets back the results of the commands it ran. Its conversation keeps only its last 20 turns: older messages, with the results of their commands, are dropped. Its scratchpad, the notes it writes itself with `yc-bench scratchpad write` or `append`, is in its system prompt at every turn. The Register's text is shown in the system prompt too, after the scratchpad, at every turn, between the lines "[Register: kept by code since the start of this run, from your commands and their results]" and "[End of Register]".

The Register gets one step per decision.
- step["action"]: {"tool": "run_command", "arguments": {"commands": [...]}}, every command the agent ran at its previous decision, in order (an empty list when it ran none; None at the first decision).
- step["result"]: a JSON string, a list of {"command": ..., "output": ...}, one per command, in the same order. Each output is the tool's result as a JSON string: {"ok", "exit_code", "stdout", "stderr"}; stdout holds the command's own JSON.
- step["seen"]: the user message of this decision (see <example_step> and prompt.py).

Example, the first decisions of a run on another seed. At decision 2, step["action"] was:
{"tool": "run_command", "arguments": {"commands": ["yc-bench market browse", "yc-bench employee list", "yc-bench company status"]}}

